<title>USA: Brunswick says FTC ends engine probe.</title>
<headline>Brunswick says FTC ends engine probe.</headline>
<dateline>LAKE FOREST, Ill. 1997-03-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brunswick Corp said Tuesday the Federal Trade Commission had concluded its investigation begun in 1993 of the company's outboard marine engine business, including its joint venture interest in Tracker Marine LP.  </p>
<p>&quot;We are pleased that the FTC has closed this matter after deciding that no action is warranted,&quot; said Brunswick chief executive officer Peter Larson.  </p>
<p>The company had been told the FTC was investigating it regarding antitrust issues, Bruswick said.</p>
<p>Brunswick shares were down 1/8 at 28-5/8.</p>
<p>((Chicago newsdesk, 312-408-8787))</p>
